Correction to the description: I removed the "+0.8% on GB300 multi-turn throughput" claim.

I re-measured with more runs on the same config: A-B-B-A, 6 warm runs per arm, plus a second run on an idle node. The difference is inside main's own run-to-run spread of 1.9-2.7%:
- main 1351.1 vs PR 1328.2 tok/s;
- idle node: main 1334.0 vs PR 1331.8;
- ITL and accept length are identical on both arms.

The PR removes host syncs from the GDN extend path, and outputs are unchanged (the deterministic exactness gate is in the description). It makes no end-to-end throughput claim. The code is unchanged.

